      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "Very little depth to this maiden so the unraced FOUR INTHE MORNING (7) gets her chance. By The Autumn Sun from an All Too Hard mare whose only previous foal has placed twice at stakes level from only four runs. Won a recent trial here in good style and looks all set for a strong debut. NETT'S GIRL (8) didn't have the best of luck and should have finished a little closer when returning from a long spell over 1200m at Port Macquarie last start. Raced once over 1400m and finished second, coming from near the tail at Taree. Can improve sharply on that first-up run. SHAKESPEARE'S GIRL (10) has struggled a bit in two 1600m races since an eye-catching second over today's journey at Tamworth in August. In the right race to bounce back to form. The chances look to end there. REDALUCA GIRL (9) and IRISH ACCOLADE (2) have raced 74 times between them without a win but on recent efforts each of them is capable of a top four finish.",
